I am a very impatient person, but I easily manage 
to farm for around 20k-30k turns; the trash 
accumulated until then seems to suffice - given some 
polypile skill - to ascend.  But even worse, you 
could write a script that takes over once you 
filled the level with puddings, doing nothing 
but attempting to move one square to the left until 
it succeeds, pick up and throw the pudding corpses 
to the left, then do the same stuff for one step 
to the right, and breaks this routine if hungry 
to try to make a move and then pick up and eat a 
pudding corpse until this suceeds.  Although I'm not 
sure whether this script could run 'forever' (leaving 
out wrapping of counters and such things), I am 
pretty sure that with quite high probability it 
could run for 1000k turns and longer undisturbed, 
and this should suffice to generate enough loot 
for everybody.  And somehow I have a feeling that, 
if such a dumb script could make a character ascendable, 
there's something not working as intended.  

Of course one can argue that there are different 
ways of winning the game, but the mere fact that 
there's no #ascend or #godmode command indicates 
that there is some intention to limit the ways 
you can win.  Hence I believe it to be in the 
spirit of the gaming design to make a judgement 
whether a particular way of winning seems intended 
or not.  However, my main point is not that this 
allows to ascend almost any character, or whether 
this possibility is intended or not, but rather that 
this particular possibility is downright ridiculous 
and not justifiable by quoting NHINRL.  One single, 
lowly brown pudding has in and of itself the potential 
of giving any char the means necessary to become a 
demigod, without need to use more than an absolute 
minimum of skills, like eat when hungry and so forth.  
I just wonder that there are no commercial farming 
industries equipping every new char with +12 HoB, 
GoP, SDSM, CoMR.  It would be almost for free.  

Actually, I'd prefer an #ascend command over this.  

